    "behaviour": {"x": 470, "y": 0, "w": 600, "fill": "blue", "size": "m", "text": "F6 decisions (product owner, 2026-11-16)\n\n1. My deeds has two tabs while invites are off: Recognised for and I reported. The Invites tab returns when invites are switched on.\n2. Self-logs get the same photo section as the deed form: up to 4, Take photo or Upload.\n3. The doer sees who reported them: \"Priya Sharma recognised you\".\n4. Editing a report: category, description and people helped can always be changed; photos can be changed for 24 hours after sending, then they lock. Who, when and where never change: they are the verification evidence. Edits are logged and the deed shows \"Edited\".\n\nAlso from the design doc: Withdraw needs confirmation and can't be undone; the deed stops counting for the doer. Self-logs are private, never earn points, and can be edited or deleted any time. Profile shows Self-log Deeds and Verified Deeds (counted reports); on your own profile both link through. Log out now lives on Profile.\n\nSample user: Priya Sharma (@priyas).\nPress Play: Profile → tap Verified Deeds → I reported → open Ahmed → Edit or Withdraw. Or tap Self-log Deeds → Log a deed."}
  },
